10. API Requirements
The API must be resource-oriented and kept small.

Do not create unnecessary endpoints. The purpose of every endpoint should be clear.

10.1 Authentication
POST /api/auth/login

Purpose:

Authenticate a user.

10.2 Deliveries
GET /api/deliveries

Purpose:

Retrieve deliveries relevant to the authenticated user/role.

POST /api/deliveries

Purpose:

Create a delivery.

GET /api/deliveries/:id

Purpose:

Retrieve delivery details.

PATCH /api/deliveries/:id/assign

Purpose:

Assign or reassign a delivery to a rider.

PATCH /api/deliveries/:id/status

Purpose:

Request a delivery status transition.

POST /api/deliveries/:id/confirm

Purpose:

Confirm a delivery after QR/barcode validation.

GET /api/deliveries/:id/events

Purpose:

Retrieve the delivery event history.

10.3 Riders
GET /api/riders

Purpose:

Retrieve available riders for dispatcher assignment.

10.4 Dashboard
GET /api/dashboard

Purpose:

Retrieve dashboard information required by the application.

