14. Security Requirements
The prototype must demonstrate basic production-minded security.

Required controls:

Passwords must never be stored as plain text.

Authentication must be enforced by the backend.

Authorization must be checked server-side.

All incoming data must be validated.

The application must not trust role information supplied directly by the frontend.

Sensitive environment variables must be protected.

Database/service-role credentials must not be exposed in frontend code.

QR/barcode confirmation must be validated on the server.

HTTPS must be used in the deployed application.

15. Real-Time Requirements
Real-time synchronization is a core prototype requirement.

Use real-time database subscriptions for important delivery updates.

The system must demonstrate this scenario:

Dispatcher assigns a delivery to Rider A.

Rider A's dashboard receives the assignment without refreshing.

Rider A updates the delivery to Picked Up.

Dispatcher dashboard updates automatically.

Rider A scans the delivery QR code.

Backend validates the delivery and Rider.

Delivery is confirmed.

Relevant dashboards update automatically.

Delivery timeline records the event.

16. QR/Barcode Requirements
Each delivery must have a unique identifier.

That identifier must be representable as a QR code.

The system must support:

QR-code generation

QR-code display

Device-camera scanning

Identification of the delivery from the scan result

Backend verification of the scanned delivery

Verification that the delivery belongs to the authenticated Rider

Verification that the delivery is in a valid state

Delivery confirmation only after successful backend validation

The QR/barcode process is part of the delivery-confirmation workflow and must not bypass backend authorization or state validation.

17. UX Requirements
The interface must prioritize clarity over visual complexity.

A user should immediately understand:

What deliveries exist

Who is assigned

Current status

What action they can perform next

17.1 Status Indicators
Use clear status indicators for:

