23. Acceptance Criteria
The Reflex prototype is acceptable when an evaluator can perform the complete required workflow through the deployed application:

Authentication
A user can log in.

The system recognizes the user's role.

Users can access only functionality appropriate to their role.

Delivery Creation
Retailer Staff can create a delivery.

The delivery contains the required customer, address, item, timestamp, status, and assignment information.

Assignment
Dispatcher can view pending/open deliveries.

Dispatcher can view available riders.

Dispatcher can assign a delivery to a rider.

Dispatcher can reassign a delivery where necessary.

Status Workflow
Rider can view assigned deliveries.

Rider can update status through permitted transitions.

Invalid transitions are rejected by the backend.

Real-Time Behavior
Assignment changes appear without manual refresh.

Status changes appear to relevant users without manual refresh.

QR/Barcode Confirmation
A delivery has a unique identifier represented by a QR code.

Rider can scan using the device camera.

Backend validates the scanned delivery.

Backend validates Rider ownership.

Backend validates the delivery state.

Valid confirmation is accepted.

Unauthorized confirmation is rejected.

Audit Trail
Important delivery events are recorded.

Events identify the event type.

Events identify the delivery.

Events identify the user who performed the action.

Events include timestamps.

Delivery history can be viewed.

Deployment
The prototype is accessible through a real URL.

The demonstration does not depend on localhost.

Production environment variables are configured correctly.

HTTPS is used.

